          "content": {
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tAfro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer & neurodivergent friendly] Tickets | 23 Nov @ The Common Press Shoreditch, London | Pay What You Can | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script async src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/7769677a7968bf74e504bc7599959c8f5cdfe69ca94b0638a17c981254064d3f3540f1cb22d8839bc7820c9608d113eb98efe7ea68fbf7cc1ac3c817446e0c56/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2026-11-03\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Afro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer &amp;amp; neurodivergent friendly]A film night for POC with niche interests. For fans of sci-fi, futuristic things, de-colonising space, mind benders, dystopias and alien vibes - with a lil discussion afterwards to talk about the film ★[soft drinks available to purchase at The Common Press + bring your own snacks]The purpose is to create a casual gathering of sci-fi film lovers who haven’t been able to take up space in a genre that’s typically predominantly white and to expand the narratives of science fiction from other cultures, featuring sci-fi films that focus on black &amp;amp; brown narratives. Beginning with a focus on Afro-sci fi, the intention is to continue watching films from other cultural identities and heritages that explore sci-fi in their own ways too. A place where it’s okay to feel off in the world &amp;amp; recreate  With an intention to set these up regularly, this is a re-launch to set the ball rolling again..  After a wonderful return last month with Crumbs, our next screening takes us to Cameroon, with Les Saignantes. Please note, this event is POC OnlyTitle: Les Saignantes [The Bleeders] Film description: Sci-Fi Erotic Horror set in Cameroon: Vampiric femmes fatales emasculate high-ranking Cameroonian officials through ancient rituals of Mevoungou [contains nudity]Trailer: https://youtu.be/kesSVI-FXjc?si=AAoF_BUwd3_H2-tlSchedule Outline:18:30 - Doors Open19:00 - Film Starts20:30 - Film ends20:40 - Discussion on film21:30 - Event ends Organiser: Niito [artist name iNKOGNiiTO] A music/visual artist and cinema projectionist - currently bleeding the concept of their artistry into reality through curating queer &amp;amp; neurodivergent friendly black &amp;amp; brown centred sci-fi film nights. Niito is starting to explore cosmic re-indiginising in micro communities. Curating spaces that de-center the white gaze through a sci-fi lens to create an alternative futuristic scene. Other key words: speculative non-fiction, decolonising space, afro nomads, befriending alienation, mundane absurdism.\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Afro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer &amp; neurodivergent friendly] Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/39678/afro-sci-fi-film-club-4-the-global-majority-queer-neurodivergent-friendly\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/42b2fcd1-b564-427f-b1e3-3105e3c8e33b.png\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Afro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer & neurodivergent friendly] Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/39678/afro-sci-fi-film-club-4-the-global-majority-queer-neurodivergent-friendly\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/42b2fcd1-b564-427f-b1e3-3105e3c8e33b.png?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Afro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer &amp;amp; neurodivergent friendly]A film night for POC with niche interests. For fans of sci-fi, futuristic things, de-colonising space, mind benders, dystopias and alien vibes - with a lil discussion afterwards to talk about the film ★[soft drinks available to purchase at The Common Press + bring your own snacks]The purpose is to create a casual gathering of sci-fi film lovers who haven’t been able to take up space in a genre that’s typically predominantly white and to expand the narratives of science fiction from other cultures, featuring sci-fi films that focus on black &amp;amp; brown narratives. Beginning with a focus on Afro-sci fi, the intention is to continue watching films from other cultural identities and heritages that explore sci-fi in their own ways too. A place where it’s okay to feel off in the world &amp;amp; recreate  With an intention to set these up regularly, this is a re-launch to set the ball rolling again..  After a wonderful return last month with Crumbs, our next screening takes us to Cameroon, with Les Saignantes. Please note, this event is POC OnlyTitle: Les Saignantes [The Bleeders] Film description: Sci-Fi Erotic Horror set in Cameroon: Vampiric femmes fatales emasculate high-ranking Cameroonian officials through ancient rituals of Mevoungou [contains nudity]Trailer: https://youtu.be/kesSVI-FXjc?si=AAoF_BUwd3_H2-tlSchedule Outline:18:30 - Doors Open19:00 - Film Starts20:30 - Film ends20:40 - Discussion on film21:30 - Event ends Organiser: Niito [artist name iNKOGNiiTO] A music/visual artist and cinema projectionist - currently bleeding the concept of their artistry into reality through curating queer &amp;amp; neurodivergent friendly black &amp;amp; brown centred sci-fi film nights. Niito is starting to explore cosmic re-indiginising in micro communities. Curating spaces that de-center the white gaze through a sci-fi lens to create an alternative futuristic scene. Other key words: speculative non-fiction, decolonising space, afro nomads, befriending alienation, mundane absurdism.\" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/39678/afro-sci-fi-film-club-4-the-global-majority-queer-neurodivergent-friendly\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"OutSavvy | Afro Sci-Fi Film Club 4 the Global Majority [queer &amp; neurodivergent friendly] | Monday 23rd November 2026 @ The Common Press Shoreditch | Pay What You Can | Find event and ticket information for The Common Press\" />\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        $(document).ready(function () {\r\n\r\n            var cookieEnabled = navigator.cookieEnabled;\r\n\r\n            // When cookieEnabled flag is present and false then cookies are disabled.\r\n            if (cookieEnabled === false) {\r\n                window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            // try to set a test cookie if we can't see any cookies and we're using \r\n            // either a browser that doesn't support navigator.cookieEnabled\r\n            // or IE (which always returns true for navigator.cookieEnabled)\r\n            if (!document.cookie && (cookieEnabled === null || /*@cc_