            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tThe films of Annette Kennerley Tickets | 06 Nov @ UCL East - One Pool Street, London | Sold Out | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script async src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/7769677a7968bf74e504bc7599959c8f5cdfe69ca94b0638a17c981254064d3f3540f1cb22d8839bc7820c9608d113eb98efe7ea68fbf7cc1ac3c817446e0c56/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2026-11-02\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Join UCL Centre for the Study of Contemporary Art, Cinenova, LUX and Spectra, Queer non fiction films for a screening of works by artist Annette Kennerley, recently digitised by MSc Conservation of Contemporary Art &amp;amp; Media students.From the late 80’s through to the late 90’s, East London based filmmaker Annette Kennerley produced a unique and deeply personal body of moving image works that explored the dynamics of queer relationships, transgender lives and experiences of motherhood.This screening includes three lesser-seen early works, produced while Annette was a student at Saint Martins College: her first 8mm film ‘Bet Lynch’s Earrings’ (1986), and videos ‘Pride and Prejudice’ (made with Debi Hall) (1988) and ‘Red Sails’ (1989). The screening also includes two of Annette’s inquiries into trans lives, the celebrated ‘Boys in the Backyard’ (1997) and ‘Kelby’ (1997). The screening will be followed by a Q&amp;amp;A and conversation between Annette Kennerley and artist / filmmaker Sweatmother.PROGRAMME:‘Pride and Prejudice’, 1988, 10minsAn agit-prop video documentary made with Debi Hall capturing some of the fight back and protests against Margaret Thatcher’s odious Clause 28 (which aimed to ban what the Conservative government called the ‘promotion of homosexuality’ in schools). The film uses footage from marches, TV clips and animated recreations.‘Red Sails’, 1989, 3minsA half-remembered lullaby from childhood haunts a new mother as she sets out to re-adjust and re-balance her old life with her new one. A sadness and longing for something lost battles with the excitement of change and the unknown.‘Boys in the Backyard’, 1997, 22minsA slice of San Francisco life in the summer of 1993. Matt and Jo sit together in their back yard and talk about their daddy/boy relationship, transgender life, love, tattoos and tomato plants.‘Kelby’, 1997, 20 mins‘I’m just a regular bloke…’ Kelby’s gender was decided for him at birth – he later put right that mistake. An intimate documentary with Kelby shot in Sydney, Australia in 1996. Born both male and female, he talks about his life and identity and becoming the person he is now. &#39;Bet Lynch’s Earrings&#39;, 1986,  3minsA little fantasy take on Queer icon Bet Lynch - legendary landlady of Coronation Street’s The Rovers Return. Loosely based on a little-known fact about Bet’s amazing earring collection. Programme duration: 1 hourThe programme is made possible through support from UCL CSCA and LUX, delivered with the support of the BFI Screen Heritage Fund, awarding National Lottery funding.\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The films of Annette Kennerley Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/40685/the-films-of-annette-kennerley\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/99638606-adf1-4150-8b43-e70d392060a2.png\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"The films of Annette Kennerley Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/40685/the-films-of-annette-kennerley\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/99638606-adf1-4150-8b43-e70d392060a2.png?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Join UCL Centre for the Study of Contemporary Art, Cinenova, LUX and Spectra, Queer non fiction films for a screening of works by artist Annette Kennerley, recently digitised by MSc Conservation of Contemporary Art &amp;amp; Media students.From the late 80’s through to the late 90’s, East London based filmmaker Annette Kennerley produced a unique and deeply personal body of moving image works that explored the dynamics of queer relationships, transgender lives and experiences of motherhood.This screening includes three lesser-seen early works, produced while Annette was a student at Saint Martins College: her first 8mm film ‘Bet Lynch’s Earrings’ (1986), and videos ‘Pride and Prejudice’ (made with Debi Hall) (1988) and ‘Red Sails’ (1989). The screening also includes two of Annette’s inquiries into trans lives, the celebrated ‘Boys in the Backyard’ (1997) and ‘Kelby’ (1997). The screening will be followed by a Q&amp;amp;A and conversation between Annette Kennerley and artist / filmmaker Sweatmother.PROGRAMME:‘Pride and Prejudice’, 1988, 10minsAn agit-prop video documentary made with Debi Hall capturing some of the fight back and protests against Margaret Thatcher’s odious Clause 28 (which aimed to ban what the Conservative government called the ‘promotion of homosexuality’ in schools). The film uses footage from marches, TV clips and animated recreations.‘Red Sails’, 1989, 3minsA half-remembered lullaby from childhood haunts a new mother as she sets out to re-adjust and re-balance her old life with her new one. A sadness and longing for something lost battles with the excitement of change and the unknown.‘Boys in the Backyard’, 1997, 22minsA slice of San Francisco life in the summer of 1993. Matt and Jo sit together in their back yard and talk about their daddy/boy relationship, transgender life, love, tattoos and tomato plants.‘Kelby’, 1997, 20 mins‘I’m just a regular bloke…’ Kelby’s gender was decided for him at birth – he later put right that mistake. An intimate documentary with Kelby shot in Sydney, Australia in 1996. Born both male and female, he talks about his life and identity and becoming the person he is now. &#39;Bet Lynch’s Earrings&#39;, 1986,  3minsA little fantasy take on Queer icon Bet Lynch - legendary landlady of Coronation Street’s The Rovers Return. Loosely based on a little-known fact about Bet’s amazing earring collection. Programme duration: 1 hourThe programme is made possible through support from UCL CSCA and LUX, delivered with the support of the BFI Screen Heritage Fund, awarding National Lottery funding.\" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/40685/the-films-of-annette-kennerley\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"OutSavvy | The films of Annette Kennerley | Friday 6th November 2026 @ UCL East - One Pool Street | Sold Out | Find event and ticket information for Spectra, Queer Non Fiction Films at UCL East\" />\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        $(document).ready(function () {\r\n\r\n            var cookieEnabled = navigator.cookieEnabled;\r\n\r\n            // When cookieEnabled flag is present and false then cookies are disabled.\r\n            if (cookieEnabled === false) {\r\n                window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            // try to set a test cookie if we can't see any cookies and we're using \r\n            // either a browser that doesn't support navigator.cookieEnabled\r\n            // or IE (which always returns true for navigator.cookieEnabled)\r\n            if (!document.cookie && (cookieEnabled === null || /*@cc_on!@*/false)) {\r\n                document.cookie = \"testcookie=1\";\r\n\r\n                if (!document.cookie) {\r\n                    window.location.replace(\"http://www.outsavvy.com\");\r\n                } else {\r\n                    document.cookie = \"testcookie=; expires=\" + new Date(0).toUTCString();\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n\r\n        });\r\n\r\n        function updateStickyTicketButton(hasTickets) {\n\n            var button = document.getElementById('stickyTicketButton');\n\n            if (!button) return;\n\n            if (hasTickets) {\n                button.href = '#checkout';\n            }\n            else {\n                button.href = '#anchor';\n            }\n        }\r\n\r\nfunction startConfirm(button, shouldValidate) {\r\n\r\n    // Run custom validation if this page has it\r\n    if (typeof validate === 'function' && shouldValidate) {\r\n        if (!validate()) {\r\n            return false;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // Prevent a second click\r\n    if (button.dataset.processing === 'true') {\r\n        return false;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    button.dataset.processing = 'true';\r\n    button.classList.add('is-loading');\r\n\r\n            return true;\r\n}\r\n\r\nwindow.addEventListener('pageshow', function() {\n\n    document.querySelectorAll('.loading-button').forEach(function(button) {\n        button.dataset.processing = 'false';\n        button.classList.remove('is-loading');\n    });\n\n});\r\n\r\n        function toggleShowPassword(clientId) {\r\n            let x = document.getElementById(clientId);\r\n            if (x.type === \"password\") {\r\n                x.type = \"text\";\r\n            } else {\r\n                x.type = \"password\";\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        function showShareModal() {\r\n            $('#shareModal').reveal({\r\n                animation: 'fadeAndPop',                   //fade, fadeAndPop, none\r\n                animationspseeed: 300,                       //how fast animtions are\r\n                closeonbackgroundclick: true,              //if you click background will modal close?\r\n                dismissmodalclass: 'close-reveal-modal'    //the class of a button or element that will close an open modal\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"57x57\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-57x57.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"60x60\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-60x60.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"72x72\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-72x72.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"76x76\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-76x76.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"114x114\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-114x114.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"120x120\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-120x120.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"144x144\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-144x144.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"152x152\" href=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/website/favicon/apple-icon-152x152.png\" /><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"180x180\" hr